{177}{[Gunther thinks a moment.]  I have no idea what the broken ring represents, but the two words are written in old Panarum--a dead language that was once used by elders of the church.  The first word means 'mirror' or 'opposite'...and the second word means 'truth'.  As for the meaning of the whole message, I'm at a loss.  I think we can assume that Mannox was trying to tell us something...}{[Gunther thinks a moment.]  I have no idea what the broken ring represents, but the two words are written in old Panarum--a dead language that was once used by elders of the church.  The first word means 'mirror' or 'opposite'...and the second word means 'truth'.  As for the meaning of the whole message, I'm at a loss.  I think we can assume that Mannox was trying to tell us something...}{}{}{}{ru 2072}
{178}{And what did YOU find, Gunther?}{}{5}{lf9 0}{181}{lf9 1}
