{296}{A message from Mannox, perhaps?  What does it mean?  Those two words are in old Panarum--a dead language once used by church elders.  The first means 'mirror' or 'opposite', and the second means 'truth'.  I have no idea what the broken ring represents.  Very, very odd...}{A message from Mannox, perhaps?  What does it mean?  Those two words are in old Panarum--a dead language once used by church elders.  The first means 'mirror' or 'opposite', and the second means 'truth'.  I have no idea what the broken ring represents.  Very, very odd...}{}{}{}{lf13 1, ru 2072}
